# What prettier is NOT allowed to touch.
#
# Prettier owns the frontend's TS/TSX/JSON/CSS/HTML. Everything below is either a language it
# cannot parse, generated output, or a file where its opinion is actively wrong.

# ── Not source ────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
node_modules/
dist/
build/
.venv/
.venv-lint/
package-lock.json
test-results/
playwright-report/
command-center/frontend/dist/

# ── Languages prettier cannot format ──────────────────────────────────────────
# Python is ruff's (prettier has no python support — the community plugin is abandoned).
*.py
# Pine Script, NinjaScript and MQL5 have no prettier parser at all.
*.pine
*.cs
*.mq5
*.mqh
*.ps1
*.sh

# ── Data, not code ────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
*.csv
*.jsonl
*.db
backtest/cache/
engines/news/data/
algos/ledger_archive/
# Machine-specific and hidden from git by `./go` with --skip-worktree; formatting it would
# un-hide it on the next status.
command-center/backend/config.json

# ── 🔴 Markdown, and this one is a DECISION with a measurement behind it ───────
# The ask was "just do all file types", and markdown is the one place that is wrong here.
#
# Prettier's markdown printer PADS TABLE COLUMNS to align the pipes. This repo's CLAUDE.md
# files are mostly wide tables with 300-character cells, so the padding is enormous and buys
# nothing a reader can see in a terminal. MEASURED 2026-08-14 on `command-center/CLAUDE.md`:
# 82 changed lines, and the file grows **22,813 → 30,844 bytes, +35%**, essentially all of it
# whitespace.
#
# ⚠ That collides head-on with a guard this repo already runs. `.claude/hooks/guard_sensitive_paths.py`
# fires on a CLAUDE.md over 40 KB that GROWS, precisely so the docs stop inflating — and it was
# deliberately changed to fire on growth rather than size because a guard that nags about work
# it should not be criticising is one people learn to dismiss. A formatter that adds 35% to
# every one of these files on every commit would trip it constantly, on whitespace.
#
# Turning this back on is a one-line delete plus `prettier --write` over the tree — but do it
# as its own commit, and check what it does to the guard first.
*.md
*.markdown
